+
+The void clause named no offered load: the base admits 0.83–0.88 at 2x
+(the load clause 1 reads), under its 0.90, and 0.92–0.93 at 0.8x, over it.
+Read as not void; the gap the arm closes is the false denies (11–43% of
+offered at `W = H`), not the admitted share alone.
+
+Limits of the reading. Timing mode ends at a seventh event inside the
+horizon, so it serves a rule only while `limit x Horizon / W` is 6 or
+less: "5 in 10 s" on a 60 s filter leaves it at once (1–3% of requests in
+timing mode, the base's answers), and reads 0.998 only on a filter whose
+horizon is 10 s. On the velocity scorecard it moves the mean by 0.0002: the
+error there is in keys of tens of events a horizon. One key's register, no
+slot protocol: the offsets must be anchored to the epoch (word0 and word1
+are two CASes), a touch rewrites up to five of them, and the hot index
+loses its top bit.
+
+### B5 larval slots: fails its rule (clause 3)
+
+`TF_LAB=1 go test -run TestLabLarva -v` (`lab/b5-larva.txt`).
+
+0. Validity holds. The adult arm against the filter on the same stream:
+   evictions 0, 0, 3,985 against 0, 0, 4,577 at loads 1.00, 1.10, 1.15
+   (13% under); relocations 149,325, 380,134, 927,332 against 148,716,
+   379,688, 932,499. Past 1.15 the two part (254,143 against 329,243
+   evictions at 1.30): the adult arm's counts there are the model's.
+1. Holds: 68.3% of live keys are larvae at every load to 1.75; cells in
+   use 55.8% at load 1.00 where the adult layout uses 84.8%.
+2. Holds: no eviction at 1.30 or 1.50; the first at 1.75 (4,314, with
+   97.7% of cells in use). Unseen touches that search: 0.4%, 0.9%, 1.3%,
+   3.4%, 11.5% at loads 1.00–1.50, against the adult arm's 22.6%, 41.7%,
+   56.9%, 69.9%, 77.0%.
+3. Fails: at load 1.00, 60.5% of metamorphoses need a move (15% allowed)
+   and 0.17% a search (3% allowed).
+
+### B5b larvae spread: fails its rule (clause 3)
+
+`TF_LARVA_SPREAD=1` (`lab/b5b-larva-spread.txt`). Clauses 0–2 as B5 (the
+same evictions and searches to within a few keys). Clause 3: 25.7% of
+metamorphoses at load 1.00 need a move (34.3% at 1.15), 0.17% a search.
+Under B5's 60.5%, over the 15% of the rule.
+
+Reported, not judged (`lab/b5-moves-split.txt`): the rule counted every
+move alike. Split at load 1.00, B5b: 74.1% of second touches grow in their
+own pair, 10.4% move inside their own line (no line loaded that the touch
+had not), 15.3% move to their other line, 0.17% search. B5: 39.4%, 45.6%,
+14.9%, 0.17%. A second touch that today is a hit of one line becomes, for
+one key in seven, an install in another line.
+
+What the arm shows whatever its verdict: on this stream two keys in three
+never get a second event, the table at design load is 56% full in words,
+and the search that 23–57% of new keys run at loads 1.00–1.15 is run by
+0.4–1.3% of them. What it costs is on the second touch, and the model
+can't price it: a word that changes kind under the slot protocol, the hit
+path telling a larva from an adult, and 35-bit times.
